Hi Thiago,

Just to add onto this, there unfortunately is no way to share information only across sub-groups in multi-species models in spOccupancy (or spAbundance), so one option would be to fit three separate msPGOcc() models and then combine/compare results of those three groups after the fact. Or, you could fit one big msPGOcc() with all species. The pros and cons of these sorts of approaches is outlined nicely from this paper back in 2014: https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/ece3.976.

Cheers,

Jeff

